# Citation metadata. GitHub reads this file and renders a "Cite this repository" button.
# The project is pre-release, so there is no date-released and no DOI yet.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Telltale in your research, please cite it as below."
title: Telltale
abstract: >-
  A local flight recorder for coding-agent sessions and a forecasting laboratory kept at
  arm's length from it. Telltale records observable coding-agent work from the surfaces the
  agent already exposes, reconstructs software-work activities, and compiles scoped
  numerical series for forecasting experiments. Every derived number carries a claim class,
  so no layer can present a value as stronger evidence than the layer that produced it.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: 0xfauzi
repository-code: "https://github.com/0xfauzi/telltale"
url: "https://github.com/0xfauzi/telltale"
license: MIT
version: 0.0.1
keywords:
  - coding agents
  - observability
  - claim class
  - software engineering research
  - time series
  - forecasting
